cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WaveSimFEM in academic research or industrial applications, please cite it as below."
title: "WaveSimFEM: A GPU-accelerated finite element framework for acoustic and elastic wave propagation in layered media"
type: software
abstract: >-
  WaveSimFEM is a GPU-accelerated finite element framework built on DOLFINx and
  PETSc for acoustic and elastic wave propagation in layered media, including
  guided and surface waves (Lamb, Rayleigh, leaky and interface waves) in layered plates
  and halfspaces with isotropic, anisotropic and viscoelastic solids coupled to inviscid acoustic
  (pressure) fluids. It
  provides rigorously stable explicit RK4 solvers, including a coupling-inclusive
  bound for fluid-solid systems, implicit Newmark solvers, absorbing sponge
  layers, exact point sensors and 2D FFT dispersion analysis from seismic to
  ultrasonic scales.
